The fault is confirmed: both leaf routers are missing `maximum-paths ebgp 2`, collapsing the dual-spine ECMP fabric to a single active path through `spine_router_0_0`. `spine_router_0_1` contributes zero forwarding — exactly the "all traffic squeezed down one path" scenario. When `spine_router_0_0` is unreachable, all inter-rack traffic fails with no failover.

